# Knight of the Reliquary: "+1/+1 for each land card in your graveyard" counts only its controller's graveyard (Bot2's LED
# discards seven Islands on turn 2 and Bot1's Knight stays 2/2) and only land cards there (Bot1's own Mishra's Bauble, sacrificed
# on turn 1, is not counted). "{T}, Sacrifice a Forest or Plains" offers the Forest and the Plains but not a Mox or the Mountain,
# the sacrificed land is a cost (in the graveyard before the search), the search finds any land card but no nonland card (Llanowar
# Elves), and the Knight is 3/3 after one land card is in the graveyard, 4/4 after two (CR 613.4c, 701.21, 701.23). It needs a
# turn without summoning sickness for {T}, hence the activations on turns 3 and 5.

